From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: burntcarrot <aadhav.n1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] sentry/kernel: add AdvanceQuantum(ns) to DeterministicScheduler

The run-burst control command (patch 7) calls sched.AdvanceQuantum(step)
with a nanosecond argument to drive time-based task wakeups during a burst
window. However DeterministicScheduler only had an AdvanceQuantum() method
on the VirtualClock (patch 1), not on the scheduler itself.

This patch adds:
  - VirtualClock.AdvanceNS(ns int64): raw nanosecond advance (unfrozen only)
  - DeterministicScheduler.AdvanceQuantum(ns uint64): advances the virtual
    clock by ns nanoseconds and pings the scheduler wakeup channel so any
    task waiting on a virtual timer that has now expired will be unblocked
    and added to the run queue on its next scheduling turn.

This is the minimal fix that makes run-burst functional. Instruction-level
granularity is handled separately in patch 23.
---
 pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_scheduler.go | 10 ++++++++++
 pkg/sentry/time/virtual_clock.go   | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_scheduler.go b/pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_scheduler.go
index 3a1bb7d66..b2a04e1c0 100644
--- a/pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_scheduler.go
+++ b/pkg/sentry/kernel/dst_scheduler.go
@@ -180,3 +180,14 @@ func (ds *DeterministicScheduler) notify() {
 	default:
 	}
 }
+
+// AdvanceQuantum advances the virtual clock by ns nanoseconds and signals
+// the scheduler wakeup channel. Used by the run-burst control command to
+// drive time-based task wakeups without waiting for a full scheduler cycle.
+//
+// Safe to call concurrently with Schedule(); the virtual clock is mutex-
+// protected and the wakeup channel is buffered.
+func (ds *DeterministicScheduler) AdvanceQuantum(ns uint64) {
+	ds.clock.AdvanceNS(int64(ns))
+	ds.notify()
+}
diff --git a/pkg/sentry/time/virtual_clock.go b/pkg/sentry/time/virtual_clock.go
index 42851c29f..f3a9c8b12 100644
--- a/pkg/sentry/time/virtual_clock.go
+++ b/pkg/sentry/time/virtual_clock.go
@@ -163,4 +163,15 @@ func (vc *VirtualClock) MonotonicNS() int64 {
 	defer vc.mu.Unlock()
 	return vc.monotonicNS
 }
+
+// AdvanceNS advances the virtual clock by an arbitrary nanosecond delta.
+// Used by DeterministicScheduler.AdvanceQuantum to drive fine-grained time
+// advancement during a run-burst window. No-op when frozen.
+func (vc *VirtualClock) AdvanceNS(ns int64) {
+	vc.mu.Lock()
+	defer vc.mu.Unlock()
+	if !vc.frozen && ns > 0 {
+		vc.monotonicNS += ns
+	}
+}
